<title>UK: Pearson names Scardino as new CEO.</title>
<headline>Pearson names Scardino as new CEO.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pearson Plc said on Thursday that Frank Barlow will be succeeded by Marjorie Scardino, who will become chief executive at the end of the year.  </p>
<p>Pearson also said that Dennis Stevenson, who is a non-executive director, is to be appointed deputy chairman with immediate effect and will succeed Michael Blakenham as chairman at the Pearson annual meeting in May next year.</p>
<p>Scardino is currently chief executive of the Economist Group, which is 50 percent owned by Pearson.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
